Layout mirrors upstream include/: the per-component headers live in
walnuts/, with walnuts.hpp the umbrella that includes them all. These
are pristine upstream copies - do not edit them; changes belong
upstream, and local needs go in bairrtt_types.h.

Previous snapshot was a10d5603939159b1eeb3fb431ea816c2e1010644
(2026-06-12), the initial import. Five headers changed (adapt, api,
config, sampler, util); the rest are byte-identical.

API drift vs that snapshot, and why none of it reaches bairrtt:
  - adapt.hpp / sampler.hpp / api.hpp: upstream unified the threaded
    adaptation and sampling drivers - AdaptWorker and ChainWorker lost
    ctor arguments; sampler.hpp's controller_loop() now takes
    SamplingConfig instead of loose tolerances, while adapt.hpp's lost
    its `latest` out-parameter and builds the vector itself; and
    detail::sample() was resigned to take SamplingConfig directly. Two
    semantic changes ride along: adapt.hpp's final publish became
    unconditional, and both loops' max-iteration test moved from a
    per-chain minimum to a cross-chain sum. All of it is the MULTI-CHAIN
    driver (detail::adapt, detail::sample, walnuts::walnuts). bairrtt
    drives AdaptiveWalnuts one chain at a time from src/irt_hmc.cpp and
    never enters that path - in fact none of these three headers is even
    in the transitive include closure of bairrtt_types.h, so they are
    never preprocessed into the build. The detail::Buffer alias adapt.hpp
    used to export is gone; bairrtt never named it.
  - util.hpp / config.hpp: new detail::leapfrog_error() and
    detail::adapt_step(), plus InitConfigBuilder::adapt_step_build(),
    a heuristic initial-step-size search. Purely additive. bairrtt
    still passes its own step_size through InitChainConfig; adopting
    the heuristic would mean calling adapt_step() in create_sampler(),
    which is a separate decision (the target there is conditional on a
    theta that has not been sampled yet).
  - The AdaptiveWalnuts -> sampler() -> WalnutsSampler lifecycle, the
    diagonal MassEstimator, the InitChainConfig(step_size, position,
    mass) ctor, and the ChainHandler callback set (on_sample /
    on_warmup / on_warmup_complete) are all UNCHANGED.

Same commit is vendored in stan4bart (inst/include/WALNUTS_VERSION).
